Software Requirements Specification
WeatherApp - Local Demonstration Version
Version 1.0
Date	  Version	Description   	Author
March 20, 2026	1.0	Initial Draft	         Oscar Franklin and Bennett Roberts 
________________________________________
1. Introduction
1.1 Purpose
This document specifies the software requirements for WeatherApp, a web-based weather information application developed for CS445 at SEMO. WeatherApp provides users with current weather conditions, forecasts, and weather-related alerts through a localhost web interface. This SRS covers the complete functionality for the demonstration version, which will run in a web browser without requiring mobile app deployment.
1.2 Document Conventions
•	Must / Shall: Indicates mandatory requirements
•	Should: Indicates recommended but not mandatory requirements
•	May: Indicates optional requirements
•	Priority Levels: High (critical for demonstration), Medium (important but not blocking), Low (nice-to-have)
•	REQ-X: Functional requirement identifier
•	NFR-X: Non-functional requirement identifier
1.3 Intended Audience and Reading Suggestions
Audience	Purpose	Recommended Sections
Instructor/Evaluator	Assess completeness and quality	All sections
Developers	Implement the system	Sections 3, 4, 5
Testers	Verify requirements	Sections 4, 5
Project Manager	Scope and planning	Sections 1, 2, 4
1.4 Product Scope
WeatherApp is a web-based weather application that retrieves and displays weather data from a public weather API. The application will run on localhost (development server) and provide a responsive interface for viewing current weather conditions, 5-day forecasts, and severe weather alerts for user-searched locations. This version is designed for academic demonstration purposes and will not be deployed to production app stores. The product will not include user accounts, saved locations, or push notifications.
1.5 References
•	OpenWeatherMap API Documentation: https://openweathermap.org/api
•	W3C Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1: https://www.w3.org/WAI/standards-guidelines/wcag/
•	IEEE Std 830-1998: IEEE Recommended Practice for Software Requirements Specifications
________________________________________
2. Overall Description
2.1 Product Perspective
WeatherApp is a new, self-contained web application. It operates as a standalone system that communicates with external weather APIs to retrieve data. The application consists of a front-end user interface (HTML/CSS/JavaScript) and a lightweight back-end proxy (Node.js or Python Flask) to handle API requests securely.

